privileged: Do not import neutron.common.utils

Each privsep daemon imports the module holding an entrypoint on first
use. The privileged ip_lib and utils modules import neutron.common.utils
for three small helpers, which drags openstacksdk, SQLAlchemy and pecan
into every neutron privsep daemon: about 28MB of RSS each.

Move read_file() and the two cidr_broadcast_address helpers into a new
privsep_safe_utils module, which neutron.common.utils re-exports, and
add a test that stops privileged modules importing neutron.common.utils.

Prompt: Mikal asked for privsep memory fixes that can be landed one at a
time and measured in devstack CI; neutron daemons are the largest.

